{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310817,"nonce":"33WwDPGuPIDqD3qXpo7JOOsVzSE=","title":"Wasm iface dispatch fixed end-to-end (commit 05b75df, 2026-06-13) — 5 stacked root causes; llama-chat wasm now reaches prefill; remaining ...","message":"**Commit 05b75df (2026-06-13).** llama-chat on wasm went from\ntrap-at-`cast(loaded.model, CausalLanguageModel)` to running load +\ntokenize + template + generation loop into prefill. Five stacked fixes:\n\n1. **`_start` wrapper** (wasm_backend.rs ~1093): synthetic wrapper calls\n   all `__vtable_init__` then `__init__` then entry. Nothing invoked\n   init hooks on wasm before — third backend with this bug class (AOT\n   was 60bbbf2).\n2. **runtime-wasm registry** (runtime-wasm/src/type_system.rs NEW):\n   iface/class vtable + ctor registries. ABI trap: linker requires\n   EXACT sig equality with the user import or it silently stubs —\n   user emits i32 ids/closure ptrs (not native i64), e.g.\n   `haxe_iface_vtable_set_slot(i32,i32,i32,i32)`.\n3. **Zero-init class allocs** (hir_to_mir build_heap_alloc): malloc'd\n   objects now zeroed per-8-byte-lane via **i64 GEPs — NOT PtrAdd**\n   (SROA only tracks GEP/Copy/Cast; PtrAdd uses dangle after malloc\n   elision → W0020 \"PtrAdd ptr not found\", broke 32 suite tests until\n   switched to GEP). Fixes Haxe null-field guarantee; was latent on\n   native (fresh zero pages), deterministic garbage on wasm.\n4. **Cross-module dispatch thunks** (ensure_cross_module_dispatch_thunk):\n   `wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr` used to fall back to RAW methods when\n   the method's IrFunction was cross-module — closure ABI prepends env\n   so callee got shifted args. Masked natively by devirtualization\n   (wasm pipeline runs skip_analysis() so no devirt). Repro:\n   field-held iface in 3-file program, `encode(String):Array\u003cInt\u003e`\n   returned [].\n5. **haxe_coerce_dynamic_to_int/float** ported to runtime-wasm —\n   were unresolved imports with return-0 host stubs, making every\n   Dynamic→Int comparison 0 (W0014 recovered-return-type path emits\n   them). Note: user imports them as (i32)-\u003ei32 not the MIR-declared\n   I64.\n\nAlso: call_indirect trusts MIR signature (RAYZOR_WASM_LEGACY_CI_RESULTS=1\nreverts); linker protects rt elem-claimed table slots from user mirror\nclobber; **name section** now flows backend→linker→wasmtime so traps\nshow Haxe symbols (huge debugging lever); `RAYZOR_WASM_DUMP=\u003cpath\u003e`\ndumps linked module.\n\n**UPDATE (commit 3a017fd, 2026-06-13): llama-chat RUNS END-TO-END on\nwasm** — loads, prefills, streams coherent tokens (exit 0; ~0.1 tok/s\nsingle-thread scalar — perf is a separate axis). Final 3 fixes after\n9f5c256: (1) tensor_binary trailing-dim broadcast `a[...,D] op b[D]`\n(RMSNorm `norm.mul(weight)` was returning null → null attention input\n→ \"KVCache.append failed\"); (2) haxe_bytes_sub/fill/blit stop unboxing\npos/len (raw file offsets mis-deref'd as boxed Dynamics → tensor name\nread from wrong offset → \"missing weight blk.N\" load roulette);\n(3) rayzor_throw_typed prints \"uncaught exception: \u003cmsg\u003e\" before\ntrapping (huge debugging lever — every Haxe throw was an anonymous\nunreachable). DEBUG METHOD that cracked it: rt_dbg/rt_dbg_n stderr\nmarkers in runtime-wasm (kept #[allow(dead_code)] in lib.rs) +\ndistinct return codes + RAYZOR_WASM_TRACE_STRINGMAP — walked the null\nbackward gather→rms_norm→mul. Deferred: location-hash type-id fallback\n(broke clone-identity), remaining unbox handle-tightening, wasm perf\n(single-thread scalar; Phase 8 = wasi-threads + i8x16 dot).\n\n**UPDATE (commit 9f5c256):** PtrAdd-no-scaling on wasm (vs Cranelift\nelement-index semantics) + never-restored shadow stack were the real\nqmatmul-OOB + load-roulette causes (workflow wf_93e68b7d-f71, binary-\nverified). Both FIXED. llama-chat wasm now loads + runs prefill through\nfusedQkvMatmul; NEXT BLOCKER: Haxe throw in KVCache.append during\nprefill. Deferred: unbox_int_from_memory tighten/remove (survey table\nin workflow output; haxe_bytes_sub pos/len = worst site; compiler-side\nfix = add Ptr-\u003eInt coerce arm in maybe_box_for_extern_call\nhir_to_mir:~24281). Location-hash type-id fallback attempted+reverted\n(broke clone-identity; unify with resolve_runtime_class_type_id first).\n\n**Earlier diagnosis (superseded but context):** llama-chat\nwasm traps are a PER-RUN ROULETTE across 4 sites, progressively deeper:\nGGUFReader.metaString throw / ArchRegistry.build validate-reject /\nLlamaArch.takeWeight map-miss throw / qmatmul OOB (the furthest run).\nAll are String/metadata map lookups. Cache mixing REFUTED by workflow\nwf_e23fa350-860 (BLADE fingerprint includes extra_defines = de-facto\ntarget key; mir.cache never touched by wasm path; only thrash +\nstdlib.bsym weak-validation caveats). Two real defects: (a)\nwasm_runner.rs unbox_int_from_memory (~:382) HEURISTICALLY derefs any\n4-aligned i32 \u003e64KB matching {type_id∈2,3} as a boxed Dynamic — 20+\nhost-fn sites (bytes handles/pos, stringmap) — misfires depend on heap\nlayout = per-run variance; (b) deterministic_class_type_id falls back\nto nondeterministic symbol-raw+1000 ids when qualified_name unresolvable\n(seen as per-run __reflect_ctor_wrap_\u003csmallN\u003e names; FNV ids are\n0x10000000+). Fix direction: exact typing at host boundary (kill\nheuristic, like subWithBase already does), deterministic fallback ids\n(hash definition location), then qmatmul. Tooling: name section +\nRAYZOR_WASM_DUMP + wasm-tools --print-offsets make frame→source fast.\nALSO: linker should hard-error when haxe_vtable_*/haxe_iface_*/\nhaxe_coerce_dynamic_* imports go unresolved (stale runtime-wasm =\nsilent registration no-op; runtime-wasm has NO build hook — manual\ncargo build needed after compiler changes).\n\nVerified gates: 132/133 haxe suite (test_exception pre-existing fail),\nnative Paris MATCH 34 tok/s, server bench 85 tok/s, /tmp/regtest\n3-file iface repro prints 5:Paris on wasm.\n\n**PERF (commit a9f24e0, 2026-06-13): wasm decode 0.12→0.27 tok/s (2.2x).**\nUser pushed: \"single-threaded SIMD can't be this slow.\" Correct. Three\nstacked causes, found by: integer micro-loop = 4x native (JIT fine) but\nmatmul = 57x → memory/opt bound not engine; then matmul-stub = 0.15s\n(matmul is 99% of fwd); then module-compile 59ms ambiguous → micro-bench\nproved cranelift OK → bisected to deps.\n(1) **Pulley interpreter, not Cranelift JIT.** [patch] pins\ncranelift-codegen 0.133 (native macOS fix) but wasmtime 43 wants 0.130 →\ncargo DROPS wasmtime-cranelift → silent Pulley fallback (~50x). cargo\ntree -i wasmtime-cranelift = absent; pulley-interpreter present. FIX:\nwasmtime+wasmtime-wasi 43→46 (git bytecodealliance release-46.0.0 branch,\ncranelift 0.133, fork merged upstream; v46 not on crates.io — branch\nonly) + repoint [patch] darmie→bytecodealliance release-46.0.0 + force\nconfig.strategy(Cranelift). wasmtime 43→46 was source-compatible (0 API\nbreakage). In v46 the crate is renamed wasmtime-internal-cranelift.\n(2) **runtime-wasm opt-level=\"s\"** (excluded from workspace → own\nprofile; pulls runtime-core at \"s\" too) crippled kernels. → opt-level=3.\n(3) opt\u003e=2 exposed LLVM wasm-SIMD miscompile of `roundf(x).clamp(-128,\n127) as i8` in q8_k quantizer: clamp lets vectorizer prove range →\ndowngrade saturating cast to plain fptosi → UB on NaN lane → planted\n`unreachable` traps (vectorization evaluates all lanes; is_nan guard does\nNOT help — both branches computed). FIX: drop the clamp (absmax already\nbounds to [-127,127], bare `as i8` is saturating) → keeps total\nfptosi.sat. memory_reservation/guard config: NO effect (shared mem\npre-reserves). Remaining single-thread: relaxed-simd dot + Q6_K SIMD;\nthen threading (8x). REGRESSION: test_copy_clone_identity now\nSIGTRAPs(133) — pre-existing type-id nondeterminism (build-order\ndependent; fails in HEAD with perf changes stashed; was 132/133 early\nsession). Same class location-hash fallback tried+reverted. Needs\ndeterministic type-id unification.\n\n**PERF push (commits d8d9180 + a9f24e0): wasm single-thread 0.12→1.18 tok/s\n(~10x), now ~6x native-scalar-1-thread (was 57x).** \"No threading? push the\nbaseline.\" Levers, in order of payoff:\n- **Q6_K×Q8_K SIMD dot (d8d9180): 4.4x (0.27→1.18).** THE big one. Q6_K\n  (attn_v+ffn_down, ~30% of weights) was the last 100%-scalar path —\n  qmatmul dequanted the full 256-elem block to f32 PER OUTPUT COLUMN then\n  scalar f32 dot. New vec_dot_q6_K_q8_K_simd128 in q6_k.rs ports native\n  dot_q6_k_q8 via the Q4 `dot16` (i32x4.dot_i16x8); qmatmul_chunk_impl\n  routes BOTH Q4/Q6 through prequant-x→Q8_K. 6-bit recon from ql nibble +\n  qh 2-bit; −32 bias → 32·Σx via bsums. read_unaligned loads. Output\n  byte-identical to dequant path (= numerically equivalent).\n- Cranelift JIT + opt=3 (a9f24e0): 2.2x — see above entry.\n- **relaxed_dot DEAD END:** i32x4.relaxed_dot_i8x16_i7x16_add (1-instr SDOT\n  analog, would replace 7-op dot16) — wasmtime 46 Cranelift aarch64 does\n  NOT lower it: 8/8 deterministic trap, with or without\n  relaxed_simd_deterministic. Don't retry on this wasmtime/arch.\n- #[inline] on the dot kernel: destabilized (reverted) — likely co-inline\n  auto-vec interaction; left non-inline.\nMETHOD CAVEAT: kernel A/B tests are INVALID under machine thrash (4 workflow\nagents + parallel cargo builds gave 3/4 spurious \"traps\"; same binary 26/26\non quiescent box). Always quiesce before wasm reliability/perf runs.\nRemaining headroom (smaller): Q4 float-tail vectorize (single-digit %, float\nreorder risk, env-gate), outer-loop hoist. Then threading (8x). Realistic\nsingle-thread ceiling ~3-4x native (wasm SIMD width + no SDOT).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_iface_dispatch_arc` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}